From 6a752699441f18c24c8f5fa9d18de2da233faac2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: llm-pt-ibm <llm-pt-ibm@ufcg.edu.br>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:30:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mlas: unpack a full 32-value block per load in the POWER
 M1 kernel

block_size=32 is the common quantization choice and what Phi-3-mini ships,
but the inner loop consumed it as two 16-value steps, repeating the load,
mask and shift. One 16-byte load covers the whole block: mergeh and mergel
of the low/high nibble vectors give values 0..15 and 16..31 respectively.

Phi-3-mini int4 end-to-end decoding: 9.01 -> 10.48 tok/s.

The microbenchmark peak moves less than this (67.9 -> 62.9 GFLOP/s at
N=8192, within run-to-run noise there) because a single 0.8 ms op is
dominated by thread-pool overhead; the end-to-end figure is the honest one.

23/23 against the NumPy reference, 17/17 numerics, 89/89 genai unit tests.
